  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports load demand forecasting and shipment volume prediction across 20 shipping lanes (Domestic FTL, Domestic LTL, Cross-Border, Intermodal) and 8 distribution hubs. Stakeholders include the S&OP Lead and Demand Planner (forecast accuracy, MAPE by lane), VP Logistics (lane utilization, backlog risk), Capacity Planner (wait hours, dock pressure), and CFO (delivered freight revenue and on-time delivery).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Forecast volume accuracy = SUM(actual_shipments) / SUM(forecasted_shipments); 0.95\u20131.05 is healthy\n- Forecast error (shipments) = actual_shipments - forecasted_shipments; under-forecast (positive) drives expedites, over-forecast (negative) leaves capacity stranded\n- Capacity utilization = capacity_utilization_pct on capacity_snapshots; >85% on cross-border signals tightness, <50% indicates over-capacity\n- Backlog = backlog_orders; rising backlog plus high utilization = capacity shortfall\n- On-time delivery rate = delivered_order_count / total_order_count on shipment_orders\n- Average transit days = avg_transit_days for delivered orders only\n- Delivered freight revenue = SUM(freight_charge_usd) FILTER (order_status = 'Delivered')\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - shipment_orders_metrics (source: shipment_orders) \u2014 dims: order_date, lane_category, origin_hub, order_status; measures: total_freight_revenue, total_weight_delivered_lbs, delivered_order_count, total_order_count, delayed_order_count, avg_transit_days, unique_lane_count, max_weight_lbs.\n  - demand_forecasts_metrics (source: demand_forecasts) \u2014 dims: forecast_month, lane_category, hub_code, model_version; measures: total_forecasted_shipments, total_actual_shipments, total_forecasted_weight_tons, total_actual_weight_tons, forecast_record_count, unique_lane_count, max_forecasted_shipments.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. lane_id, lane_name, destination_hub, capacity_utilization_pct, backlog_orders, avg_wait_hours).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show monthly forecasted vs actual shipments by lane category for the trailing 12 months.",
    "How has delivered freight revenue trended month-over-month by origin hub?",
    "Top 10 lanes by total actual shipments last quarter and what was their forecast accuracy?",
    "Which lane categories have the highest delayed order count this quarter \u2014 where is service quality slipping?",
    "Top 10 lanes by average capacity utilization with backlog orders greater than 10 \u2014 where are we capacity-constrained?",
    "How does average transit days for delivered orders compare across Domestic FTL, LTL, Cross-Border, and Intermodal?",
    "What is the monthly forecast accuracy ratio (actual / forecasted shipments) by model version?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in delivered order count?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT order_date, MEASURE(delivered_order_count) AS delivered_order_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.shipment_orders_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY order_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has delayed order count changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT order_date, MEASURE(delayed_order_count) AS delayed_order_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.shipment_orders_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY order_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What has been the peak predicted shipment count for month each month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT forecast_month, MEASURE(max_forecasted_shipments) AS max_forecasted_shipments",
        "FROM {fqn}.demand_forecasts_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY forecast_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How many distinct forecasts appeared each month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', forecast_month) AS month, COUNT(DISTINCT forecast) AS distinct_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.demand_forecasts",
        "GROUP BY 1",
        "ORDER BY 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "Which lanes have the highest total *?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT lane_name, SUM(*) AS record_count, SUM(weight_lbs) AS total_weight_lbs",
        "FROM {fqn}.shipment_orders",
        "WHERE order_status = 'Delayed'",
        "GROUP BY lane_name",
        "ORDER BY total_weight_lbs DESC",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total predicted shipment count for month over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT forecast_month, SUM(forecasted_shipments) AS total_forecasted_shipments",
        "FROM {fqn}.demand_forecasts",
        "GROUP BY forecast_month ORDER BY forecast_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average capacity utilization percentage changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, AVG(capacity_utilization_pct) AS avg_capacity_utilization_pct",
        "FROM {fqn}.capacity_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    }
  ],
